r nomination process","ruling elder election","session prescreening nominees","mandatory sequence BCO 24-1","divorce and church office","session discretion"],"standard_of_review":"discretion_and_judgment","review_standards":["discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["2019-3"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A serving deacon nominated for ruling elder complained that his session removed his nomination before BCO 24-1 instruction or examination. The SJC held the session erred by adding an unwritten pre-examination 'vetting' removal and that Northwest Georgia Presbytery erred in approving it: BCO 24-1's sequence—instruction and examination before the session determines eligibility—is mandatory. The ruling reserved the session's sound discretion and the treatment of frivolous or clearly disqualified nominees. The complaint was sustained and remanded for adjudication consistent with the decision."}},{"id":"bco:19-13--case:cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Frazier v. Nashville Presbytery","year":2018,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:19-13--case:cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md:occ-b7d24e6d8bb3","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga46_2018__2016-11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["same-sex attraction","homosexuality","BCO 31-2 investigation","strong presumption of guilt","due diligence","great discretion","committee on judicial business","recusal","appearance of impropriety","indictment","complaint denied","standards of review","BCO 39-3.3 deference"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2016-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC denied a complaint challenging Nashville Presbytery's decision not to indict a teaching elder for allegedly sinful teaching on homosexuality and same-sex attraction. The adopted judgment held that the 147-page record showed Presbytery fulfilled its BCO 31-2 investigatory duty and did not show it erred in judgment when it declined process; the complaint was denied 20-0-1. Concurring opinions raised concerns about committee recusal, record clarity, and exegetical uses of Scripture, but they were separate and did not alter the denial."}},{"id":"bco:19-13--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/mississippi-valley__016.html","record_id":"rpr_exception:rpr/exc/mississippi-valley__016.html","type":"RPR exception","title":"Mississippi Valley: Reasons for rescission of intern status not recorded.","year":2025,"disposition":"raised","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/mississippi-valley__016.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/mississippi-valley__016.html","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:19-13--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/mississippi-valley__016.html:occ-d02265a91c29","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/mississippi-valley__016.html","repository_path":"rpr/exc/mississippi-valley__016.html","locator":{},"excerpt":"Reasons for rescission of intern status not recorded.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/mississippi-valley__016.html"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:19-13--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/korean-northwest__106.html","record_id":"rpr_e